  "id": "getcomputedstyle",
  "support": "a",
  "note": "JavaScript apps in a window have `getComputedStyle`, read one property at a time from the tree: animated properties as they are now, sizes, margins, padding and border widths as laid out, the rest as cascaded with lengths in pixels. Shorthands, custom properties and pseudo-elements read an empty string, and so does everything in a browser (web canvas) build. Silk code reads a node's computed style from the tree.",
  "evidence": "modules/js/tests/src/tests.silk (getComputedStyleReadsTheTree)"
 },
